<% seo title: "Privacy", description: "What Blendolo keeps, who sees your photos, how long we keep them and how to delete everything at once." %>
<div class="page prose">
  <%= render "pages/page_header", chip: "Privacy", title: "Your photos, your call",
        lead: "No account, no ads, no tracking. Your kit lives behind a private link, and you can delete it all at once." %>

  <h2>What we keep</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your answers about your hands, and how your hands feel today.</li>
    <li>Your photos: today's photo, and an old photo if you choose to bring back a signature look.</li>
    <li>Colours read from your photo. Your phone reads them; we only keep the colour codes.</li>
    <li>The looks you pick, your routine and any share links you make.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't ask for your name, email or phone number.</p>

  <h2>Who sees your photos</h2>
  <p>YouCam, the try-on service from Perfect Corp, uses your photos to make the previews. It removes its copies within 30 days. Nobody else sees them unless you share a link that includes photos.</p>

  <h2>Code the photo page loads</h2>
  <p>On the photo page, your browser loads the face checking code from jsDelivr and the face model file from Google Cloud Storage. Like any website, they see your IP address. Your photo never goes to them: the checks run in your browser.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>30 days from your last visit, or 7 days if you choose that when you start. After that, your kit and its photos are deleted for good.</p>

  <h2>Delete everything</h2>
  <p>Every kit has a "Delete everything" button. It deletes your photos, answers and links at once. Our hourly database backups keep your answers and links, not your photos, for up to 2 days after that. YouCam deletes its copies within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Share links</h2>
  <p>You choose who a link is for and whether it shows photos. A link stops working after 30 days, and you can switch it off any time.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Two small cookies, no trackers. One remembers your kit on this device so you can come back to it. The other keeps forms safe.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <%= render "pages/contact" %>
</div>
